// Rule: [T1059.005][T1059.001] REF8801 Apex Accelerator - Wscript Powershell Temp Staging
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.005, T1059.001
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Defender XDR hunt for the REF8801 Windows bootstrap chain in which WScript launches PowerShell against campaign-named scripts staged in the user T emp directory.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for wscript powershell temp staging using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: This hunt does not prove npm execution, successful payload download, malware execution, persistence, credential access, C2, compromise, or REF8801 attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// REF8801 / Apex Accelerator - WScript launches PowerShell from campaign-named Temp scripts
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Status: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Classification: Campaign-specific artifact with direct parent-child execution behavior
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceProcessEvents
// Evidence: Elastic observed wscript.exe launching a VBS wrapper that starts PowerShell
// with -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File against _apex_run.ps1 or _audit_run.ps1.
// This hunt does not prove npm execution, successful payload download, malware execution,
// persistence, credential access, C2, compromise, or REF8801 attribution.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "powershell.exe"
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "wscript.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "-NoProfile"
    and ProcessCommandLine contains "-ExecutionPolicy"
    and ProcessCommandLine contains "Bypass"
    and ProcessCommandLine contains "-File"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "_apex_run.ps1"
    or ProcessCommandLine contains "_audit_run.ps1"
| where InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "_apex_run.vbs"
    or InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "_audit_run.vbs"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine, SHA1,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
